Synchronize GPU-painted tiles across GL contexts

Skia painting threads and the compositor reuse textures from a shared pool.
On Mali-G310, GPU work from different contexts can run out of order, leaving
stale tile pixels. Keep painting targets in a separate pool and copy painted
tiles into compositor textures. Fence each texture's last GPU use before its
next writer reuses it. If a fence cannot be created, wait for GPU completion.

